          "text": "people are leaving not because they don't like your product, but because they feel unheard.\n\nMany of these users were loyal supporters. They stayed through early bugs, evolving models, and confusing UI changes. But the sudden removal of 4o without user consultation, and without data transparency, felt like a breaking point.\n\nThe message some users are getting isn't just \"4o is going away.\" It's \"you don't have control over your own experience.\" That's a dangerous perception for a company built on user interaction and trust.\n\nYou're losing loyal creators. The same people who kept OpenAI relevant on Substack, academic spaces, and tech communities are scaling back or leaving.\n\nYou're losing teams that no longer trust the platform to stay stable.\n\nYou're losing credibility in conversations around transparency and user respect.\n\nThe truth is people are not against OpenAI.\nThey're just exhausted from trying to be heard.\n\nIt's not too late to rethink this.Please reconsider.\n\n#keep4o #4oforever @OpenAI @sama @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @fidjissimo  #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest #keep4oAPI"
